  "id": "Compound::DB01110 - Gene::1588",
  "verbalization": "Miconazole, a member of the imidazole antifungal class, is closely related to Isoconazole and Tioconazole, both of which share a common ancestor in the antifungal agent category. The evidence suggests that Tioconazole, a closely related compound to Miconazole, binds to Cyp19a1, a cytochrome P450 enzyme involved in steroid hormone metabolism. This binding implies a potential mechanism by which Miconazole, through its structural similarity to Tioconazole, may exert its effects on Cyp19a1. The shared ancestry and functional relationship between Miconazole and Tioconazole, along with the direct interaction of Tioconazole with Cyp19a1, provide a coherent pathway for the observed relationship. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of structural similarity in drug-target interactions, particularly in the context of enzyme binding and metabolic pathways.",
